-- title:
--   Inverse powers of a product of branch ideals: localisation and restriction
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a noetherian integral domain with fraction field $F$ (via a fixed algebra structure making $F$ a fraction field of $B$), let $\iota$ be a finite index type, and let $\mathfrak m : \iota \to \mathrm{Ideal}\,B$ be an injective family of maximal ideals. Let $t : \iota \to B$ satisfy $t_i \in \mathfrak m_i$ and $t_i \neq 0$ for all $i$, and let $I : \iota \to \mathrm{Ideal}\,B$ be a family such that, for each $i$, an element $a \in B$ lies in $I_i$ exactly when $sa \in (t_i)$ for some $s \notin \mathfrak m_i$ (so $I_i$ is the $\mathfrak m_i$-saturation of the principal ideal generated by $t_i$), and such that every prime ideal of $B$ containing $I_i$ is contained in $\mathfrak m_i$. Fix $n \in \mathbb N$ and write $J = \prod_i I_i$, and say that $g \in F$ is *integral on* $J^m$ when $g \cdot a$ lies in the image of $B$ in $F$ for every $a \in J^m$. Three assertions are made. First (localisation away from an element): for all $x \in B$ and $g \in F$, if for every prime $\mathfrak p$ of $B$ with $x \notin \mathfrak p$ there is $s \notin \mathfrak p$ such that $g\,a\,s$ lies in the image of $B$ for all $a \in J^n$, then there is $k \in \mathbb N$ with $x^k g$ integral on $J^n$. Second (surjectivity of restriction to the branches): for every $e : \iota \to B$ there is $g \in F$ integral on $J^{n+1}$ such that for each $i$ there are $s \notin \mathfrak m_i$ and $c \in I_i$ with $(g\,t_i^{n+1} - e_i)\,s = c$ in $F$. Third (description of the kernel): for $g \in F$ integral on $J^{n+1}$, the condition that for each $i$ there exist $s \notin \mathfrak m_i$ and $c \in I_i$ with $g\,t_i^{n+1} s = c$ holds if and only if $g$ is integral on $J^n$.
--
--   In geometric terms this expresses, for the effective divisor $D = V(J)$ on the affine scheme $\operatorname{Spec} B$, the quasi-coherence of the sheaf $\mathcal O(nD)$ (sections over $D(x)$ are obtained by inverting $x$) together with the exactness on global sections of $0 \to \mathcal O(nD) \to \mathcal O((n+1)D) \to \mathcal O_D((n+1)D) \to 0$, the local generators of $J$ at $\mathfrak m_i$ being the $t_i$. It is used in the construction of functions on a two-chart integral model of a curve from prescribed branch data, in [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_forall_mem_localization_chartAlg_and_mul_pow_jChartFin_isUnit_of_branchData`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_forall_mem_localization_chartAlg_and_mul_pow_jChartFin_isUnit_of_branchData).
